What this licence covers, and what it does not

The text above covers this repository's own files: the adapter and the test
runners under waterbox/, the build files, the documents, and the test
program generator under tests/.

The patches under patches/ are changes to Gearcoleco and are under
Gearcoleco's licence, the GNU General Public License version 3 or later.

Gearcoleco itself (extern/gearcoleco, by Ignacio Sanchez,
https://github.com/drhelius/Gearcoleco) is under the GNU General Public
License version 3 or later; its text is extern/gearcoleco/LICENSE.

The built package (gearcoleco.chimeraCore) is Gearcoleco with these
patches and this adapter, so it is distributed under the GPL version 3 or
later. It contains, inside Gearcoleco: Blip_Buffer and Sms_Apu by Shay Green
(LGPL-2.1-or-later, conveyed under the GPL), miniz (public domain), and the
F18A's GPU program by Matthew Hagerty (BSD-3-Clause, licenses/
F18A-BSD-3-Clause.txt). Every component, its terms and its source are listed
in waterbox/package-licenses.json and travel inside the package.

The package contains no BIOS, no ROM of Coleco's and no game. The user
brings the ColecoVision BIOS and, for the ADAM, the EOS and SmartWriter ROMs.
